{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghrnmoV3f7vkkB35SgLo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011tLQkKv2eeedhp2gFDc47V","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"grep -n \"rng(seed\\|^- \\`E.rng\\|E.tones\\|E.recolor\\|E.sprite(\" API-INDEX.md | head; sed -n 403,450p API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-300","description":"Read renderer API and rng"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5086,"cache_read_input_tokens":212442,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5086},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f6976d6c-e5f5-464d-af16-4195491a03f7","uuid":"c64a8875-03db-430b-9e37-557f4efb15f9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:07:25.164Z","request_id":"req_011CghrnmYrAriAbpSbg9S8m","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_011tLQkKv2eeedhp2gFDc47V":{"command":"grep -n \"rng(seed\\|^- \\`E.rng\\|E.tones\\|E.recolor\\|E.sprite(\" API-INDEX.md | head; sed -n 403,450p API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-300","description":"Read renderer API and rng"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011tLQkKv2eeedhp2gFDc47V","type":"tool_result","content":"179:- `E.rng(s)`: a seeded random stream: const R = E.rng(42); R() gives 0..1, the same numbers for the same seed (mulberry32)\n190:- `E.tones(c, strength = 1)`: five shades of a color for painted-looking pixel art: { deep, sh, base, lt, hi }. Shadows drift toward blue-violet, highlights toward warm yellow (strength 0..2, default 1).\n210:- `E.sprite(rows, colors = {}, scale = 1)`: Pixel sprite written as strings. Each character is one pixel; colors maps a character to a hex color; '.' and ' ' are transparent. scale (whole number) enlarges each pixel. const COIN = E.sprite(['.yy.', 'yYYy', 'yYYy', '.yy.'], { y: '#f0b020', Y: '#fff0a0' }); Draw it with r.sprite(x, y, z, COIN) (depth sorted) or px.sprite(g, COIN, sx, sy).\n216:- `E.recolor(spr, map)` †: a copy of a sprite with its colors swapped (palette swaps: the second player, a hurt flash, a stronger enemy): recolor(spr, { '#3a8a4a': '#8a3a4a', h: '#e0b040' }), each key a color or one of the sprite's own characters\n## 9. Renderer\n\n- `r.H`: the screen's height in game pixels\n- `r.W`: the screen's width in game pixels\n- `r.actor(x, y, z, drawFn, o = {})`: Queue a character. drawFn(g, ox, oy) must draw with (ox, oy) as the projected position of world point (x, y, z). The engine adds outline, rim light, hit flash, afterimages and x-ray silhouettes. opts: {outline=true, rim=true, flash=false, alpha=1, xray=false, gh\n- `r.actor({ xray })`: true shows the actor's hidden part (a translucent tint with a 1-px outline, r.xrayColor and r.xrayOutline; a checker in E.style.trans 'dither') wherever a wall, a prop or shape at least chest high, or anything queued with hides is drawn in front of it (not one rising less than\n- `r.actor({ hides })`: true: this actor counts as an x-ray occluder even when no x-ray actor asked for actors\n- `r.actor({ ghost })`: ghost.owner (any {x, y, z}, usually the actor itself) keeps its afterimages sorted behind the live body\n- `r.actor({ every, key })`: every: n, key (any object, the character's own): its finished image is drawn again for n - 1 frames before drawFn runs again, at the place it is now (a background character animating at a lower rate, as classic games' townsfolk do: a phone's frame keeps the time for the \n- `r.actor({ wrap })`: [w, h], as r.sprite's: a world that wraps round shows the actor across each edge it crosses\n- `r.actorNow(x, y, z, drawFn, o = {})`: draw an actor at once, over what is drawn so far, not sorted by depth (a pass of the game's own: a body falling into a void painted over the level), with r.actor's options (outline, flash, alpha, ...)\n- `r.bh`: the buffer's height (H + 2)\n- `r.box(g, x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, top, side)`: extruded box prop (crate, pedestal, table). Call inside a queue fn with its g.\n- `r.bw`: the buffer's width (W + 2: a pixel of margin each side for the sub-pixel camera)\n- `r.ctx`: the low-resolution buffer's 2D context: draw on it with E.px\n- `r.decal(fn, o)`: draw on the floor before the queue. opts.emissive (0..1) makes it glow under GPU lighting\n- `r.glowDisc(g, cx, cy, rad, color, a)`: glow halo from a cache: additive light rings (alpha style) or a dithered disc (dither style). a = 0..1 strength\n- `r.groundArc(x, y, r0, r1, a0, a1, color, alpha = 1, z = 0, g = this.tgt)`: a band of a ring on the ground from radius r0 to r1 and angle a0 to a1 (radians): melee telegraphs, sight cones\n- `r.groundDisc(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a dithered disc lying on the ground (radius in world units, z its height): shadows, auras, area attacks\n- `r.groundPts(x, y, rad, n = 18, z = 0)`: n screen points round a circle of radius rad on the ground at (x, y), height z: the outline of a ring or a fan\n- `r.groundRing(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a ring lying on the ground (radius in world units)\n- `r.marker(x, y, z = 0, o = {})`: an objective marker over a world point: a bobbing diamond (and its label) while it is on screen, an arrow at the screen's edge pointing to it while it is off (offscreen: false hides it then). o: { label, color: '#ffd040', offscreen: 'arrow' }\n- `r.overlay(fn)`: draw fn(g) on top of everything, in screen pixels (HUD, dialog, menus)\n- `r.pick(sx, sy)` †: what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicked(), input.pointer()) in the last frame, front to back: the pick values of the actors, sprites, props and queued draws given one (r.actor(x, y, z, fn, { pick: unit })), each where its pixels went (an actor's dra\n- `r.prop(name, x, y, z, o = {})` †: set dressing from E.prop: r.prop('torch', x, y, z, { size, color, flip, light: true, halo: true, bias, hides, footprint }) feet on the world point; flames animate and glow. light: true also adds a warm light to game.lights. A prop at least chest high (E.HEIGHTS.c\n- `r.queue(x, y, z, fn, o)`: queue a depth-sorted draw. fn(g) draws into g. opts: {bias, occluder, hides, xray, emissive, solid (hides a glow behind it), footprint} occluder: a wall (x-ray silhouettes show through it, it sorts as a block). hides: only lets x-ray silhouettes show through it (props, s\n- `r.shadow(x, y, rad, alpha = .5, color = '#0c0818', z = 0)`: soft contact shadow under a character: a cached dithered ellipse, correct for the current view. z = height of the surface it falls on (0 = floor; the top of a block or platform otherwise)\n- `r.shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: Queue a shape standing at (x, y, z), feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor: r.shape(id | entry, x, y, z, o). o: { facing (radians, where its front points; default PI/2, south, as written), scale, mats: { slot: material }, flip (mirror it x to -x before\n- `r.sightCone(obs, o = {})` †: an observer's view on the ground: a dithered fan fov wide (radians) about its facing, out to range, cut short where the map hides a body's chest (map.ray, the height rules), draped over the ground below. o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye, color: '#ffe080', a\n- `r.sky(colors, o = {})`: background of dithered color bands, top to bottom: r.sky(['#0b1030', '#3b2d6b', '#e0806a']). Call first in draw.\n- `r.sprite(x, y, z, spr, o = {})`: Queue a pixel sprite (from E.sprite) standing at world point (x, y, z). Depth sorted like an actor. opts: { flip, anchor: 'bottom' (feet on the point, default; E.shapeSprite's: its own feet) | 'center' | 'top', glow: 0..1, bias, flash, outline, alpha, xray, ghost \n- `r.starfield(o = {})`: scrolling star dots for space and night skies. opts: { count: 70, speed: 30 px/s, dir: 'down' | 'up' | 'left' | 'right', colors, layers: 3, seed }\n- `r.text(str, x, y, color = '#ffffff', o)`: HUD text in screen pixels, drawn on top and never lit: r.text('SCORE 120', 4, 4, '#fff', { align, scale, outline })\n- `r.textAt(x, y, z, str, color = '#ffffff', o = {})`: text floating at a world point (names, prompts): r.textAt(x, y, z, 'OPEN', '#ffe08a')\n- `r.tgt` †: current draw target for ground helpers (switches during GPU info and overlay passes)\n- `r.view`: the view this frame is drawn in (the game's, with zoom and turn)\n- `r.visible(x, y, z = 0, mx = 60, up = 30, down = 90)`: is a world point near the visible area? margins in pixels (characters extend upward from their feet)\n- `r.w(x, y, z = 0)`: world -> buffer pixel coords\n- `r.game`: its game; items: this frame's queue (sorted by depth when the frame ends)\n- `r.glowMask = true` †: false lets emissive glows show over everything under canvas lighting (cheaper: the default keeps walls and bodies in front of a glow dark)\n- `r.gpu = false` †: true during a frame drawn with GPU lighting (draw code can check r.gpu)\n- `r.ix`, `r.iy`: the camera's whole-pixel offset this frame (a world point is at r.w(x, y, z) on the buffer)\n- `r.outline = '#140c1c'`: the color of the 1-pixel outline round every actor\n- `r.rim = '#ffe2b8'` †: the rim light's color on actors' lit edges\n- `r.rimAlpha = .28` †: its strength 0..1\n- `r.xrayColor = '#8fe3ff'` †: the default color of x-ray silhouettes\n- `r.xrayOutline = '#e8fdff'` †: the default 1-px outline round a silhouette's hidden part (null for none)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f6976d6c-e5f5-464d-af16-4195491a03f7","uuid":"73032337-8dcb-4142-8591-a9d5d8cb8938","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:07:25.184Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"179:- `E.rng(s)`: a seeded random stream: const R = E.rng(42); R() gives 0..1, the same numbers for the same seed (mulberry32)\n190:- `E.tones(c, strength = 1)`: five shades of a color for painted-looking pixel art: { deep, sh, base, lt, hi }. Shadows drift toward blue-violet, highlights toward warm yellow (strength 0..2, default 1).\n210:- `E.sprite(rows, colors = {}, scale = 1)`: Pixel sprite written as strings. Each character is one pixel; colors maps a character to a hex color; '.' and ' ' are transparent. scale (whole number) enlarges each pixel. const COIN = E.sprite(['.yy.', 'yYYy', 'yYYy', '.yy.'], { y: '#f0b020', Y: '#fff0a0' }); Draw it with r.sprite(x, y, z, COIN) (depth sorted) or px.sprite(g, COIN, sx, sy).\n216:- `E.recolor(spr, map)` †: a copy of a sprite with its colors swapped (palette swaps: the second player, a hurt flash, a stronger enemy): recolor(spr, { '#3a8a4a': '#8a3a4a', h: '#e0b040' }), each key a color or one of the sprite's own characters\n## 9. Renderer\n\n- `r.H`: the screen's height in game pixels\n- `r.W`: the screen's width in game pixels\n- `r.actor(x, y, z, drawFn, o = {})`: Queue a character. drawFn(g, ox, oy) must draw with (ox, oy) as the projected position of world point (x, y, z). The engine adds outline, rim light, hit flash, afterimages and x-ray silhouettes. opts: {outline=true, rim=true, flash=false, alpha=1, xray=false, gh\n- `r.actor({ xray })`: true shows the actor's hidden part (a translucent tint with a 1-px outline, r.xrayColor and r.xrayOutline; a checker in E.style.trans 'dither') wherever a wall, a prop or shape at least chest high, or anything queued with hides is drawn in front of it (not one rising less than\n- `r.actor({ hides })`: true: this actor counts as an x-ray occluder even when no x-ray actor asked for actors\n- `r.actor({ ghost })`: ghost.owner (any {x, y, z}, usually the actor itself) keeps its afterimages sorted behind the live body\n- `r.actor({ every, key })`: every: n, key (any object, the character's own): its finished image is drawn again for n - 1 frames before drawFn runs again, at the place it is now (a background character animating at a lower rate, as classic games' townsfolk do: a phone's frame keeps the time for the \n- `r.actor({ wrap })`: [w, h], as r.sprite's: a world that wraps round shows the actor across each edge it crosses\n- `r.actorNow(x, y, z, drawFn, o = {})`: draw an actor at once, over what is drawn so far, not sorted by depth (a pass of the game's own: a body falling into a void painted over the level), with r.actor's options (outline, flash, alpha, ...)\n- `r.bh`: the buffer's height (H + 2)\n- `r.box(g, x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, top, side)`: extruded box prop (crate, pedestal, table). Call inside a queue fn with its g.\n- `r.bw`: the buffer's width (W + 2: a pixel of margin each side for the sub-pixel camera)\n- `r.ctx`: the low-resolution buffer's 2D context: draw on it with E.px\n- `r.decal(fn, o)`: draw on the floor before the queue. opts.emissive (0..1) makes it glow under GPU lighting\n- `r.glowDisc(g, cx, cy, rad, color, a)`: glow halo from a cache: additive light rings (alpha style) or a dithered disc (dither style). a = 0..1 strength\n- `r.groundArc(x, y, r0, r1, a0, a1, color, alpha = 1, z = 0, g = this.tgt)`: a band of a ring on the ground from radius r0 to r1 and angle a0 to a1 (radians): melee telegraphs, sight cones\n- `r.groundDisc(x, y, rad, color, alpha = 1, z = 0)`: a dithered disc lying on the ground (radius in world units, z its height): shadows, auras, area attacks\n- `r.groundPts(x, y, rad, n = 18, z = 0