{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghufMTB56SuJRCja5WB7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01W2VkcQxNGBTkYA2T3Mmwpb","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > about.json <<'EOF'\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-04 05:02:59\",\n    \"source\": \"Smash TV (Williams Electronics arcade game, 1990)\",\n    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",\n    \"genre\": \"Twin-stick arena shooter (arcade), 1-4 player co-op\",\n    \"perspective\": \"Fixed single-screen arena from a high three-quarter studio camera (threequarter view, pitch 55); Overhead (topdown) as a Settings option\",\n    \"tech\": \"my-3D2dge handoff v0.85.2 (commit 4390a98, full edition with the arcade module) with 4 small patches; AI Hub session client aihub-session 1.4.0; plain JavaScript in one IIFE; Node 24.22.1 and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests\",\n    \"artDirection\": \"The engine's native PS1-style pixel look (320x240 expanded, HD Humanoid rigs, textured TileMap, canvas lighting) dressed as a retro-future TV studio: neon, chrome, marquee bulbs, sponsor logos, confetti, spotlights and a jumbotron\",\n    \"animation\": \"The engine's procedural rig system (Humanoid and Blob, E.MOVES attacks, poses, flips, landings) plus new motion: the mime's trapped-in-a-box joint post-process, cable drops, boss part tweens, wheel spin easing, TV channel flips\",\n    \"audio\": \"All synthesized in code: 8 original songs in the engine's notation with layers and 14 stings, about 70 custom sound effects, and Animalese/Simlish Babble voices from a small formant synth for the host, co-host, announcer, bosses, contestants and the crowd\",\n    \"online\": \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world mode, 1-4 players (the Lightning Round); local co-op 1-4 on one screen\",\n    \"testing\": \"Headless Node suites driving game.advance and game.debug (including a scripted playthrough of the whole game), Playwright browser checks on the deliverable over file://, and the AI Hub harness on a 127.0.0.1 server on an OS-picked port\",\n    \"research\": \"Read the engine handoff docs (API.md, AI_GUIDE.md sections, ASSETS.md, API-INDEX.md by grep) and the AI Hub protocol README and harness; no web research on the source\",\n    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\",\n    \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n    \"usage\": \"unknown\"\n  },\n  \"questions\": {\n    \"testingFeedback\": [\"How many issues did testing catch?\", \"How many were critical or game breaking?\", \"Most helpful test?\", \"Least helpful test?\"],\n    \"engineFeedback\": [\"What did you like most?\", \"Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\", \"Most important thing you built yourself?\", \"Hardest part?\", \"What did you change in the engine?\", \"One thing you would change?\"],\n    \"promptFeedback\": [\"What did you like most?\", \"What was confusing?\", \"Hardest thing to do?\", \"What would you change?\"]\n  },\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\"unknown\", \"unknown\", \"unknown\", \"unknown\"],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\"unknown\", \"unknown\", \"unknown\", \"unknown\", \"unknown\", \"unknown\"],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\"unknown\", \"unknown\", \"unknown\", \"unknown\"],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"MASH TV\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Mash 'em! Cash 'em! Survive the show.\",\n    \"description\": \"A 1-4 player twin-stick arena shooter inside the deadliest game show on TV: blast through studio rooms of goons and robots, grab cash and absurd prizes, keep the ratings up and survive to the Season Finale.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Shooter\",\n    \"source\": \"Smash TV\",\n    \"series\": \"\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"WASD/left stick move · mouse/right stick aim & fire · Space/L2 slide · E/R1 Showstopper · Q/L1 Showboat\",\n    \"tags\": [\"arcade\", \"co-op\", \"top-down\", \"pixel art\", \"comedy\", \"boss fights\"]\n  }\n}\nEOF\ncd .. && no