{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghwCZm53j6k9D7SmU16e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Writing the final About/exit-interview content while the suite finishes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":407,"cache_read_input_tokens":605074,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":407},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f6976d6c-e5f5-464d-af16-4195491a03f7","uuid":"818072b1-d11b-4fc2-98a4-c5a99aa98277","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:04:28.544Z","request_id":"req_011CghwCZSDkrbQQyqCG5DHG"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghwCZm53j6k9D7SmU16e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Xd3pVAgCjwEb4hBJnwi8Xp","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='src/about.json'; a=json.load(open(p))\na['sourceInformation']['testing']=\"One command (npm test) runs 20 suites: 18 headless Node suites driving game.advance and game.debug (including room-sweep over all 26 rooms and a scripted playthrough of the whole game) plus 2 Playwright suites: the deliverable over file:// at 1280x720, 1920x1080 and a touch phone, and the AI Hub harness 4 times (2 players; 4 players at 150 ms +-50 ms with 5% loss; host leaving; a server copy) on an in-process 127.0.0.1 server on an OS-picked port. Screenshots only for looks.\"\na['sourceInformation']['usage']=\"unknown (no usage figures are visible to the model in this session)\"\na['testingFeedback']=[\n \"About 14 real issues: contestants could not walk out of exit doors; enemy painters crashed on a missing render state (an error every frame); a missing hpPct field; waves advancing before queued spawns arrived; boss phase coroutines killed by the runner right after their intro (bosses never attacked); the recap and ending scenes keeping flags from the previous visit (the run stalled after Episode 2); a party popper bursting twice; the attract mode's boss reel jumping into the recap; an unseeded Math.random in boss cash; tunings not persisting where storage is absent; the camera fit clamped so the arena was cropped; title menu overlapping the logo; lower third covering the session card buttons; illegible wheel labels.\",\n \"4 would be game breaking: no way out of a room after a clear, the per-frame draw crash, bosses that never attacked, and the run stalling at the second Prize Recap.\",\n \"The scripted whole-game playthrough (two bots on the left path through all three episodes, the Green Room, Ending B, initials and Top Earners): it found the recap stall and proved every system connects. The room-sweep, which found the boss coroutine bug, was a close second.\",\n \"The first version of the enemy-count convergence check in the netcode loopback: it compared one instant of host and client during a spawn burst, so it measured latency rather than mirroring, and had to be rewritten as an average.\"]\na['engineFeedback']=[\n \"The amount that comes free and works headless: fixed-step game.advance with exact determinism, Humanoid rigs that look good dressed with a few options, the standard pause/settings/controls menus, canvas lighting, and scenes with fades. Writing tests that play the whole game in seconds was easy.\",\n \"Yes: I assumed the camera fit would land near zoom 1, but the threequarter view's base scale is about 1.5, so my clamp cropped the arena; I guessed r.overlay text glyphs like the multiplication sign and middle dot exist in the tiny font (they don't); and game.addPlayer also fires allowJoin's onJoin, which I didn't expect.\",\n \"The shared-world netcode (host-authoritative world, client mirror with local prediction, snapshots, claims and hurts) and the boss framework with coroutine phases; also the PlayStation/Xbox glyph icons, since the font has no face-button symbols.\",\n \"Fitting a fixed single-screen arena to an expanding screen (map.bounds, base view scale and zoom interact), and keeping arrows as aim keys in play while the engine's menus need them to navigate.\",\n \"Four small patches, each marked MASH TV PATCH: E.HOOKS exposed so presets can switch per player before the Shell reads navigation; the glyphs setting defaulting to PlayStation with an Xbox option applied to every player; E.Arcade initials and continue reading any player's input; and an audio bus getter so the Babble voices obey volume and mute.\",\n \"A built-in per-player input-preset stack for menus versus play (and face-button glyph icons in the font), so twin-stick games don't need a hook to make arrows aim in play and navigate in menus.\"]\na['promptFeedback']=[\n \"It is concrete about what done means (single file, exit interview shape, attract mode, dev sliders, controller-first rules) and the plan it pointed to was detailed enough to build from directly.\",\n \"The relationship between 'feature-complete demo' and the plan's very large scope (18 rooms, 3 multi-phase bosses, shared-world netcode) at medium effort; and whether Source Information's Plan field should name the file or its author.\",\n \"Making shared-world multiplayer pass the hub harness while keeping the same game playable locally with 1-4 players and an attract mode, all in one file.\",\n \"Say how much of a large plan to prioritise when time is limited, and give the expected exit-interview usage source (the model cannot see token or cost figures).\"]\njson.dump(a,open(p,'w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Write final feedback into about.json"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":407,"cache_read_input_tokens":605074,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":407},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f6976d6c-e5f5-464d-af16-4195491a03f7","uuid":"4f712cf5-ccf8-4e3b-b2f2-a0a3070715a1","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:04:46.091Z","request_id":"req_011CghwCZSDkrbQQyqCG5DHG","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Xd3pVAgCjwEb4hBJnwi8Xp":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='src/about.json'; a=json.load(open(p))\na['sourceInformation']['testing']=\"One command (npm test) runs 20 suites: 18 headless Node suites driving game.advance and game.debug (including room-sweep over all 26 rooms and a scripted playthrough of the whole game) plus 2 Playwright suites: the deliverable over file:// at 1280x720, 1920x1080 and a touch phone, and the AI Hub harness 4 times (2 players; 4 players at 150 ms +-50 ms with 5% loss; host leaving; a server copy) on an in-process 127.0.0.1 server on an OS-picked port. Screenshots only for looks.\"\na['sourceInformation']['usage']=\"unknown (no usage figures are visible to the model in this session)\"\na['testingFeedback']=[\n \"About 14 real issues: contestants could not walk out of exit doors; enemy painters crashed on a missing render state (an error every frame); a missing hpPct field; waves advancing before queued spawns arrived; boss phase coroutines killed by the runner right after their intro (bosses never attacked); the recap and ending scenes keeping flags from the previous visit (the run stalled after Episode 2); a party popper bursting twice; the attract mode's boss reel jumping into the recap; an unseeded Math.random in boss cash; tunings not persisting where storage is absent; the camera fit clamped so the arena was cropped; title menu overlapping the logo; lower third covering the session card buttons; illegible wheel labels.\",\n \"4 would be game breaking: no way out of a room after a clear, the per-frame draw crash, bosses that never attacked, and the run stalling at the second Prize Recap.\",\n \"The scripted whole-game playthrough (two bots on the left path through all three episodes, the Green Room, Ending B, initials and Top Earners): it found the recap stall and proved every system connects. The room-sweep, which found the boss coroutine bug, was a close second.\",\n \"The first version of the enemy-count convergence check in the netcode loopback: it compared one instant of host and client during a spawn burst, so it measured latency rather than mirroring, and had to be rewritten as an average.\"]\na['engineFeedback']=[\n \"The amount that comes free and works headless: fixed-step game.advance with exact determinism, Humanoid rigs that look good dressed with a few options, the standard pause/settings/controls menus, canvas lighting, and scenes with fades. Writing tests that play the whole game in seconds was easy.\",\n \"Yes: I assumed the camera fit would land near zoom 1, but the threequarter view's base scale is about 1.5, so my clamp cropped the arena; I guessed r.overlay text glyphs like the multiplication sign and middle dot exist in the tiny font (they don't); and game.addPlayer also fires allowJoin's onJoin, which I didn't expect.\",\n \"The shared-world netcode (host-authoritative world, client mirror with local prediction, snapshots, claims and hurts) and the boss framework with coroutine phases; also the PlayStation/Xbox glyph icons, since the font has no face-button symbols.\",\n \"Fitting a fixed single-screen arena to an expanding screen (map.bounds, base view scale and zoom interact), and keeping arrows as aim keys in play while the engine's menus need them to navigate.\",\n \"Four small patches, each marked MASH TV PATCH: E.HOOKS exposed so presets can switch per player before the Shell reads navigation; the glyphs setting defaulting to PlayStation with an Xbox option applied to every player; E.Arcade initials and continue reading any player's input; and an audio bus getter so the Babble voices obey volume and mute.\",\n \"A built-in per-player input-preset stack for menus versus play (and face-button glyph icons in the font), so twin-stick games don't need a hook to make arrows aim in play and navigate in menus.\"]\na['promptFeedback']=[\n \"It is concrete about what done means (single file, exit interview shape, attract mode, dev sliders, controller-first rules) and the plan it pointed to was detailed enough to build from directly.\",\n \"The relationship between 'feature-complete demo' and the plan's very large scope (18 rooms, 3 multi-phase bosses, shared-world netcode) at medium effort; and whether Source Information's Plan field should name the file or its author.\",\n \"Making shared-world multiplayer pass the hub harness while keeping the same game playable locally with 1-4 players and an attract mode, all in one file.\",\n \"Say how much of a large plan to prioritise when time is limited, and give the expected exit-interview usage source (the model cannot see token or cost figures).\"]\njson.dump(a,open(p,'w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Write final feedback into about.json"}}}
