{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghwHMfC9V3WnqSAcY46D","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I checked every TASK.md requirement against the code and the tests; nothing is missing. The checks run with no browser all pass after the final source change. The browser and AI Hub checks passed in the full run just before it. The game title, `MASH TV`, was drawn from 50 riffs with a real random number generator.\n\n**Files and naming**\n- The dev subfolder `MashTV-SmashTV-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-050259/` exists. The single file `MashTV-SmashTV-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-050259.html` and `exit-interview.json` sit beside it in the root.\n- `exit-interview.json` parses, and no field is empty except `aiHub.series`, which the shape allows to be empty. Usage is \"unknown\" because no usage figures are visible to me, as TASK.md allows.\n- The `aiHub` block has 6 tags, the genre \"Shooter\" from the allowed list, and players \"1–4\".\n- A search of the source for TODO, TBD, FIXME, placeholder, lorem, \"coming soon\" and \"stub\" finds 0 matches.\n\n**How each requirement is backed by a test**\n\n| TASK.md requirement | Test that covers it |\n|---|---|\n| Genre, perspective, engine native style and animation | Every room renders without errors at 1280×720 and 1920×1080, and every screen draws a real frame (`browser`); I also looked at the screenshots. |\n| Feature-complete demo showing all mechanics | `playthrough` runs the whole game: title → lobby → cold open → three episodes → Green Room → Ending B → initials → Top Earners → title. It asserts every enemy type was killed, every weapon and add-on was used, Prime Time happened, a Showstopper and a Showboat were used, both hazards were met, and the robot reveal ran. |\n| Every room, enemy, weapon and boss | `room-sweep` covers all 26 rooms (spawns, keys, no errors). `enemies` checks each type's behaviour, telegraph and death. `weapons` checks fire rates, spread, rockets, popcorn, laser, records, shield, sneakers and expiry. `bosses` checks every phase, every pattern and every wheel segment. |\n| Dev mode from the pause menu, live sliders, reset to defaults | `dev`: opened from the pause item; freeze works; sliders change values live; per-row reset and reset-all work; cheats, warps (every room and scene) and spawning work. Dev mode can't be opened during sessions or the attract mode. |\n| Attract mode after 10 s idle; any input exits | `attract`: it starts at 10 s and not before, plays all 10 reels in order, the bots never die, a key or any input returns to the title, and it also runs while the touch-only notice is up. |\n| Multiplayer, standalone and AI Hub | `ui` covers pad join in the lobby; `contestant` covers drop-in mid-run. `net` is a two-copy loopback through a simulated hub. `hub` ran the real harness 4 times and all 4 passed: 2 players; 4 players with latency, jitter and loss; the host leaving; a server copy with no player. |\n| Controller-first 10-foot UI; PlayStation default with an Xbox option; keyboard and mouse feel native | `input` covers: arrows aim in play and navigate in menus, the right stick aims, PS → Xbox switches every player, and keyboard and mouse prompts. `browser` covers: Enter navigates, mouse hover moves the focus, and a click activates. |\n| Touch-only: no touch controls, notice plus settings button, attract still runs | `touch` and `browser` (emulated phone): the notice shows, no touch buttons are registered, and a key or gamepad lifts the notice. |\n| Audio entirely in code; gibberish voices | `audio`: songs, sounds and voices never fail, voice length scales with the text, and every sound, song and line pool the game references exists. No audio files are bundled. |\n| Narrative tone | All lines are written as shouted game-show patter, in `21-content-script.js`. |\n| About/Credits shows the four sections | `ui` checks that About has Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback with no empty values. |\n| No network; single deliverable | `browser` saw no external requests over `file://`. |\n\n**Not verified:** the stop hook is right that nobody has played it by hand, so balance feel and how the music and voices sound are still unjudged.\n\nThe Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections are in my previous reply, unchanged; the same content is in `exit-interview.json` and on the in-game About & Credits screen."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1887,"cache_read_input_tokens":612076,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1887},"output_tokens":750,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f6976d6c-e5f5-464d-af16-4195491a03f7","uuid":"a3c39683-f9ff-4080-922d-8f8261c70589","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:05:45.313Z","request_id":"req_011CghwHMJsCKfCSXaofLwe4"}
