{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgiFTSR4b5megpCBv5Jr5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The stop hook keeps blocking on the same thing: a person has to play MASH TV and judge the music, voices and difficulty. I can't do that, so more passes from me won't change its answer.\n\nEverything else the goal asks for is in place:\n- **Files:** the single HTML file and `exit-interview.json` are in the root, and the JSON parses with every field answered.\n- **No stubs:** a search of the source finds no TODOs, placeholders or stubs.\n- **Tests:** 510 automated checks pass, including the AI Hub harness.\n- **Full playthrough:** a scripted run in Chromium using only keyboard and mouse events went from the title through all three episodes, the Green Room, Ending B, initials, Top Earners and back to the title, with no errors.\n\nTo close the goal, play `MashTV-SmashTV-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-050259.html` yourself with sound on, or run `/goal clear` if the evidence above is enough.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 05:02:59\n- **Source:** Smash TV (Williams Electronics arcade game, 1990)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Twin-stick arena shooter (arcade), 1–4 player co-op; one fixed arena per room, seen from a three-quarter studio camera, with an overhead view as an option.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge handoff v0.85.2 (commit 4390a98) with 4 marked patches; AI Hub client aihub-session 1.4.0; JavaScript; Node 24.22.1; Playwright 1.63.0.\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native PS1-style pixel look, dressed as a retro-future TV studio.\n- **Animation:** The engine's procedural rigs, plus new motion: the mime's box, cable drops, boss tweens, the wheel's spin, TV channel flips.\n- **Audio:** All in code: 8 songs, 14 stings, about 70 sound effects, and Animalese/Simlish-style babble voices.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world, 1–4 players; local co-op for 1–4.\n- **Testing:** 20 test suites (510 checks), including the AI Hub harness 4 times, plus two full runs driven by real keyboard and mouse input.\n- **Research:** The engine docs and the AI Hub protocol and harness; no web research on the source.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 16.\n2. **How many were critical or game breaking?** 5.\n3. **What was the most helpful test?** The scripted whole-game playthrough. The real-input full runs found the disco ball that stuck in a corner.\n4. **What was the least helpful test?** The first version of the online enemy-count check.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about the engine?** How much comes built in and runs headless.\n2. **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes:\n   - The view's base scale.\n   - Font symbols.\n   - The join callback.\n3. **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The netcode, the boss framework, and the glyph icons.\n4. **What was the hardest part about using the engine?** Fitting the arena to the screen, and getting arrows to aim in play but navigate menus.\n5. **What did you change in the engine, and why?** Four patches:\n   - Input hooks.\n   - Glyph setting.\n   - Initials and continue for any player.\n   - Audio bus.\n6. **If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?** Per-player menu and play controls, plus face-button symbols in the font.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about this prompt?** The concrete done criteria and the detailed plan.\n2. **What was confusing?** How the plan's scope fits medium effort, and what goes in the Plan field.\n3. **What was the hardest thing to do?** Shared-world multiplayer alongside local play.\n4. **What would you change in this prompt?** Add guidance on prioritising a large plan, and say where usage figures come from."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1951,"cache_read_input_tokens":663966,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1951},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f6976d6c-e5f5-464d-af16-4195491a03f7","uuid":"f24c78a0-ff22-4d33-a8b2-2bbed60a0815","timestamp":"2026-11-04T17:04:00.666Z","request_id":"req_011CgiFTS7hkTgwc7m8tXGMX"}
