 episodes, 18 rooms, 3 multi-phase bosses, Green Room, two endings, recaps, continue, high scores | Real-input run: title → all episodes → Green Room → Ending B → initials → Top Earners → title, with 0 errors. Second real-input run → Ending A. Scripted playthrough confirms every enemy type, power-up and hazard is reached |\n| Dev mode from the pause menu; live sliders for key variables; reset to defaults | 25 sliders, cheats, actions, warps, spawns, debug overlays | Opened from the pause menu with a real mouse click; a slider changed and was reset; dev suite |\n| Attract mode after 10 s idle; any input exits | 10 reels of the real game played by bots that cheat | 11 s of real idle started it and a keypress exited; attract suite |\n| Controller-first 10-foot UI; PlayStation glyphs with an Xbox option; native keyboard and mouse; prompts follow the last input used | Glyph icons, menus at most 6 items, hover moves focus, click activates | Input, UI and browser suites; real keyboard and mouse sessions |\n| No dense web-style screens | Paged screens, big text | Screenshots |\n| Touch-only device: \"Controller or keyboard required\", the settings button, attract still runs | Implemented | Emulated phone in the browser suite; touch suite |\n| Writing style like the source | Shouted game-show patter throughout | `21-content-script.js` |\n| Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback in the chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen | Implemented | UI suite checks all four sections are on About |\n| `exit-interview.json` in the exact shape, every field answered | Implemented | Parses; every field filled (`series` is empty by definition) |\n| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | — | Source search finds none |\n| Testing behind one command that prints only failures and a count | `npm test` | 510 passed, 0 failed |\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 05:02:59\n- **Source:** Smash TV (Williams Electronics arcade game, 1990)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Twin-stick arena shooter (arcade), 1–4 player co-op. A fixed single-screen arena seen from a three-quarter studio camera, with an overhead view as an option.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge handoff v0.85.2 (commit 4390a98) with 4 marked patches; AI Hub client aihub-session 1.4.0; JavaScript; Node 24.22.1; Playwright 1.63.0.\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native PS1-style pixel look, dressed as a retro-future TV studio.\n- **Animation:** The engine's procedural rigs, plus new motion for the mime's box, cable drops, boss tweens, the wheel's spin and TV channel flips.\n- **Audio:** All in code: 8 songs, 14 stings, about 70 sound effects, and Animalese/Simlish-style Babble voices.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world, 1–4 players; local co-op for 1–4.\n- **Testing:** 20 suites with 510 checks, including the AI Hub harness 4 times. Two full playthroughs driven only by real keyboard and mouse input, one ending at Ending A and one at Ending B.\n- **Research:** The engine docs and the AI Hub protocol and harness; no web research on the source.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 16.\n2. **How many were critical or game breaking?** 5: no way out of a room, a crash on every frame, bosses that never attacked, a stall at a recap screen, and a disco ball stuck in a corner.\n3. **Most helpful test?** The scripted whole-game playthrough. The real-input full runs found the stuck disco ball.\n4. **Least helpful test?** The first version of the online enemy-count check.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What I liked most:** How much is built in and runs headless.\n2. **Stuck or guessed wrong?** Yes: the view's base scale, symbols missing from the font, and the join callback.\n3. **Most important thing I built myself:** The netcode, the boss framework and the glyph icons.\n4. **Hardest part:** Fitting the arena to any screen, and making the arrow keys aim in play but navigate menus.\n5. **What I changed in the engine:** Four patches: input hooks, the glyph setting, initials and continue for any player, and an audio bus.\n6. **One thing I'd change:** Per-player menu and play controls, and face-button symbols in the font.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What I liked most:** Concrete done criteria and a detailed plan.\n2. **What was confusing:** How the plan's scope fits medium effort, and what goes in the Plan field.\n3. **Hardest thing to do:** Shared-world multiplayer alongside local play.\n4. **What I'd change:** Guidance on prioritising a large plan, and where usage figures should come from."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1740,"cache_read_input_tokens":669886,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1740},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f6976d6c-e5f5-464d-af16-4195491a03f7","uuid":"26579a2e-69e2-45a2-9d4c-21df2321f98d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T17:04:56.528Z","request_id":"req_011CgiFWnkm7CVZDGEAmXZmQ"}
